Drop the bundled jq toolchain in favour of jq.bzl

lib/jq.bzl already re-exports the rule from jq.bzl, and that rule resolves
jq.bzl's own toolchain type, so the toolchain bundled here is no longer
what any jq() target uses. It is still registered for every platform in
its own JQ_PLATFORMS table, which is a second, older copy of the same
data: it pins jq 1.7 and has no Windows arm64 entry, so it fails to
resolve on that host and takes unrelated targets with it.

Removing it leaves one source of truth. jq.bzl moves to 0.6.1, which
carries every platform this table used to provide.

This drops @aspect_bazel_lib//lib:jq_toolchain_type, which is public API.
Anything depending on it directly should use @jq.bzl//jq/toolchain
instead. v3 has already removed jq from this repository, so this brings
2.x in line rather than inventing a direction.

